-- 116_june_kb_creator_profile.sql — teach June the creator profile / portfolio / directory (2026-09-28).
-- She told a member "I don't have the exact limit on portfolio uploads" — the answer (12) lived only in
-- components/PortfolioManager.tsx (PORTFOLIO_MAX). Keep this line in step with that constant.
-- Directory rules mirror lib/directory-listing.ts.
insert into agent_kb (topic, content) values
('creator_profile', $kb$CREATOR PROFILE & PORTFOLIO (for logged-in members): Members build their profile at Account → Profile (madekulture.com/account/profile). A portfolio holds up to 12 photos. Members can frame (crop) each shot, drag to reorder, replace a photo, and mark sensitive work as 18+. Before the first upload they confirm they own the rights to the images, everyone shown is 18 or older and consented, and the content follows the studio's content standards. The studio can hide a portfolio photo that doesn't meet those standards. At 12 photos they'll need to remove or replace one to add another.$kb$),
('creative_directory', $kb$CREATIVE DIRECTORY: Members can be listed in the Creative Directory so other creatives can find and message them. To appear, turn on "List me in the creative directory" at Account → Profile, and the profile needs: a name, a short bio, at least one role (photographer, model, stylist, etc. — brands don't need a role), and at least one of a portfolio photo, a link, or an Instagram handle. If someone opted in but can't find themselves, one of those is usually missing — the profile page shows a checklist of what's left. Browsing the directory requires being listed yourself; turning the listing off also turns off access to browse. Members choose separately whether their email and phone are shown to other members.$kb$);
